00:53:35.433 --> 00:53:37.050
Years and years.

00:53:37.050 --> 00:53:37.883
So I'm like the wrong guy,

00:53:37.883 --> 00:53:39.530
because I don't know how bad it is,

00:53:39.530 --> 00:53:40.769
but I can only imagine it's pretty bad.

00:53:40.769 --> 00:53:42.370
- It's not that it's bad.

00:53:42.370 --> 00:53:45.080
It's that nobody here can speak to

00:53:45.080 --> 00:53:48.570
the desperation of going
somewhere this Saturday night.

00:53:48.570 --> 00:53:52.513
That has been eliminated from
the youth lexicon in New York.

00:53:55.300 --> 00:53:57.870
- I think in New York at that time

00:53:57.870 --> 00:54:01.413
the celebrity scene was a
little bit (sighs) grittier.

00:54:04.750 --> 00:54:07.633
And the celebrity scene drove it.

00:54:09.630 --> 00:54:11.620
The first thing that I ever wanted to do

00:54:11.620 --> 00:54:13.280
in the night life was go to Sky,

00:54:13.280 --> 00:54:15.100
Sky Bar, you remember that place?

00:54:15.100 --> 00:54:16.450
So that was like the first
thing I wanted to do.

00:54:16.450 --> 00:54:18.020
I wanted to go see fuckin',

00:54:18.020 --> 00:54:21.150
I wanted to see like Leonardo DiCaprio.

00:54:21.150 --> 00:54:22.547
- And who he was with.

00:54:22.547 --> 00:54:25.770
- And like what they were
smoking, you know what I'm saying?

00:54:25.770 --> 00:54:27.480
And Kate Moss.

00:54:27.480 --> 00:54:29.870
And they were just like out
there, you know what I mean?

00:54:29.870 --> 00:54:30.843
And like who knows,

00:54:30.843 --> 00:54:34.870
I don't know what that celebrity
clique is like right now.

00:54:34.870 --> 00:54:36.270
- [Gary] Plus everyone's a celebrity.

00:54:36.270 --> 00:54:37.103
- Yeah I guess so.

00:54:37.103 --> 00:54:39.199
You know what it is maybe?

00:54:39.199 --> 00:54:40.163
Ah.

00:54:41.030 --> 00:54:43.460
I mean this is a theory,
it could be wrong.

00:54:43.460 --> 00:54:45.523
- [Gary] It's a hypothesis.

00:54:45.523 --> 00:54:47.230
- It's just not exclusive anymore.

00:54:47.230 --> 00:54:48.770
There's zero exclusivity,

00:54:48.770 --> 00:54:51.864
everything is tracked and
traced and documented.

00:54:51.864 --> 00:54:53.600
- And edited.

00:54:53.600 --> 00:54:55.040
And also leads to different behavior

00:54:55.040 --> 00:54:56.617
when you know that you're being filmed.

00:54:57.931 --> 00:55:02.618
- There is no uncertainty when
you walk into the VIP room.

00:55:02.618 --> 00:55:04.753
- [Gary] How different is metal right now?

00:55:05.690 --> 00:55:06.690
- [John] Versus what?

00:55:06.690 --> 00:55:07.713
- 1987.

00:55:09.060 --> 00:55:09.893
Same shit?

00:55:11.040 --> 00:55:13.460
- [John] I think it's
definitely a little bit softer.

00:55:13.460 --> 00:55:15.420
- Yeah, everything has
to be softer, right?

00:55:15.420 --> 00:55:17.027
Like that's just the punch line.

00:55:17.027 --> 00:55:21.500
That's good in some ways, and not.

00:55:21.500 --> 00:55:23.110
- You know it's the same thing like

00:55:23.990 --> 00:55:27.840
you know the hip hop game is
definitely different dude,

00:55:27.840 --> 00:55:28.810
it's just definitely different.

00:55:28.810 --> 00:55:33.500
Like I grew up listening to
Naz and Wu Tang and Mob Deep

00:55:33.500 --> 00:55:35.960
and you know Black Moon
and like that shit.

00:55:35.960 --> 00:55:38.100
- Black Moon.
- How good is Black Moon?

00:55:38.100 --> 00:55:39.827
Probably one of the
best albums of all time,

00:55:39.827 --> 00:55:41.083
like I think so.

00:55:42.603 --> 00:55:45.790
My hip hop interests,
like when I work out,

00:55:45.790 --> 00:55:47.314
I listen to all the new shit.

00:55:47.314 --> 00:55:50.393
But like when I'm at home
listening to hip hop,

00:55:51.640 --> 00:55:54.127
my interests stopped after like '96.

00:55:54.127 --> 00:55:55.908
- That's what happens.

00:55:55.908 --> 00:55:57.690
It's the same reason there
are some 70 year olds

00:55:57.690 --> 00:56:00.390
only listening to fuckin'
The Rolling Stones.

00:56:00.390 --> 00:56:02.656
Like that's the game.

00:56:02.656 --> 00:56:04.330
- I don't know man, I think that there's--

00:56:04.330 --> 00:56:06.370
- [Gary] I promise you that's the game.

00:56:06.370 --> 00:56:07.355
- You think?

00:56:07.355 --> 00:56:09.010
- It's old man talk.

00:56:09.010 --> 00:56:09.910
- But listen dude.

00:56:12.470 --> 00:56:15.000
The sound changed, drastically.

00:56:15.000 --> 00:56:16.050
- Everything changes.

00:56:17.790 --> 00:56:20.770
Do you know what a restaurateur from 1947

00:56:20.770 --> 00:56:22.180
thinks about a meatball place?

00:56:22.180 --> 00:56:23.970
- [Michael] I wonder. (chuckles)

00:56:23.970 --> 00:56:26.130
- Let's leave it at that,
let's leave it at that.

00:56:26.130 --> 00:56:27.020
Bro, thank you so much,

00:56:27.020 --> 00:56:29.070
this was one of my favorite episodes bro.

00:56:29.980 --> 00:56:30.983
- [Michael] Good times.

00:56:32.518 --> 00:56:34.040
- Usually I say you keep asking questions,

00:56:34.040 --> 00:56:35.170
we'll keep answering them.

00:56:35.170 --> 00:56:36.900
You keep watching, we'll keep hanging out.

00:56:36.900 --> 00:56:39.390
See ya! (laughs)

00:56:39.390 --> 00:56:40.240
That was amazing.

